Hi all, Christie I have been immersed in the ctmm literature in preparation for my masters work, and thus think I can answer this question.  I'm sure Chris will also see this and correct me if I'm wrong!!

My understanding is an aKDE, based on a random movement model (iid) will reduce to a KDE only if there is no autocorrelation structure remaining in the dataset (i.e. if the data is thinned enough).

I may be totally wrong, but taking a stab at it!  Can anyone confirm this?  Robin

